-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       That Sinking Feeling
  Publisher   Sunteam, 2017
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        That Sinking Feeling (2017-08-02)(Sunteam)(48K-128K).tap
  MD5         5123adf2c0e828a380b9e260942def4a

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every block, figure and
              object, with its picture behind them: the wreck on the title and
              six underwater scenes, changing with the room by the set's own
              rules. Layer 2 for the scenery and the picture, sprites for the
              figures; the game's ULA+ palette off, as the set is painted for
              the Spectrum's colours. Source: Enhanced colours: Ynicky
              (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: figures and objects are hardware sprites in their own
              colour over the original screen, the plots run at 28 MHz, which
              pays for the hooks; the tape's 128K version with its AY music;
              the tape's loading screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); Enhanced colours, a menu option, off
              by default, from the Spec256 set; one tested cheat

  Note        Keys: any key starts, Q rise, O left, P right (redefinable by
              the game's table: none offered). The original look with the
              clash gone: the game draws figures straight on the screen, and
              in a cell of scenery a figure took that cell's colour. Here
              figures and objects are hardware sprites in their own pale
              yellow over the original screen, with the game's own ULA+
              palette on a Next. 128K tape, AY music. Fits a 1MB Next,
              Enhanced included. Known issues: pace in JNext against the
              original, 4 rooms x 3 seeds, game state in lockstep: whole runs
              default -0.90 to +0.01, Enhanced -0.90 to +0.69 percent; slowest
              20-update stretch default +0.44, Enhanced +1.99 percent.
              Missing: natural play past the first rooms (others by a test
              poke); hardware untested, ULA+ included.

